# Outfit window: every look of the game (client/MANIFEST.md "Owned and locked lists", BASE.md 38). The 10.98 outfit window packet lists only what the character owns; modules/game_outfit/outfit.lua now also lists every outfit, mount, aura and shader of the server's wardrobe catalogue (server wardrobe.lua, sent on the cosmetics opcode 225 and kept by the overlay module game_unlocks), the ones not owned greyed out with their unlock source in the tooltip. They can be looked at but not worn: Ok is disabled while a part in use is locked and accept() sends nothing then (the server refuses them anyway, Game::playerChangeOutfit). Presets with a locked part are greyed. "Only mine" (data/styles/40-outfitwindow.otui, now through tr()) works on every list and is kept per character and list (game_unlocks); it no longer resets when the row changes. Cards show the look facing south, zoomed to fill the card (game_lookpreview.fitCard, the sprite anchors of the character select). The rule is UnlocksCore of game_unlocks (unlocks_core_test.lua); without that module the window lists what the packet sent, as before. Lua and OTUI only. Applies after 0001-0059.
